abstract: >-
  PIREUS is an autonomous operator foundry, hardware-capability ontology engine,
  and verifiable reinforcement learning compiler framework designed for the Sounio
  programming language ecosystem. It operates at the intersection of non-associative
  Cayley-Dickson hypercomplex algebras, formal silicon microarchitecture ontologies
  (x86_64 AVX-512, NVIDIA SM121 Blackwell, Apple Silicon, and AMD Alveo U250 FPGAs),
  interactive theorem proving in Lean 4 and Koka, and group-relative policy
  optimization (GRPO). PIREUS enforces strict, non-delegable semantic authority:
  external machine learning models propose untrusted mathematical operators and
  lowering schedules, while Sounio-native executables verify well-formedness,
  classify equivalence under the GL(4,2) semidirect gauge quotient group, and
  compute deterministic binary compiler-as-a-reward signals.
keywords:
